PART 2: IAM (Identity and Access Management)

IAM is one of the most important AWS services for any DevOps or Cloud Infrastructure Engineer. Nearly every AWS interview includes IAM questions because it underpins authentication, authorization, and secure access.

What is IAM?

Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) is a global AWS service used to securely control who can access AWS resources and what actions they can perform.

IAM answers two questions:

Who are you? (Authentication)
What are you allowed to do? (Authorization)
