IAM Best Practices
1. Enable MFA

Always enable Multi-Factor Authentication for privileged users.

2. Follow Least Privilege

Give only the permissions required.

Bad:

AdministratorAccess

Good:

EC2 Start

EC2 Stop
3. Use Roles

Never store AWS access keys inside code.

4. Rotate Credentials

Regularly rotate:

Passwords
Access keys
Secrets
5. Use Groups

Avoid assigning permissions individually whenever possible.

6. Root Account

Never use the root account for daily work.

Use it only for tasks such as:

Closing the account
Changing billing information
Recovery actions
